  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column of the receipts/disbursements statement (p6; left half p5). That column eliminates 110,000 of interfund transfers (100,000 in pupil transportation, 10,000 in extracurricular) and leaves 36,182 General-to-Nutrition transfer printed as a disbursement line; recorded as transfers_out 36,182 (not in disbursements), so the printed disbursement total 3,824,527 includes transfers_out. Beginning cash is fund balance as originally reported 2,263,158; restatement -17,865 (note J) recorded as adjustment (restated beginning 2,245,293). Roll-forward: 2,263,158+4,065,949-3,788,345-36,182-17,865=2,486,715. Business-type (Nutrition Fund, p7-8): beginning 17,865 (as restated) + receipts 81,161 - disbursements 110,861 + transfer 36,182 = 24,347; measure recorded as cash since cash basis. Balance sheet uses Statement of Net Position Total column (includes the business-type column), p1. Detail: General Fund budget schedule is by function only (not itemized); hidden transfers (Pupil transportation 100,000; Activities support 10,000) moved to other financing in detail; General Fund expenditure total 3,587,902 includes other financing lines (-36,182, -100,000, -10,000). Depreciation fund total receipts 112,197 includes the 100,000 transfer; Activity fund total receipts 128,757 includes the 10,000 transfer. Combining schedule p13: Nutrition Fund column is all zero (omitted). No Nutrition Fund budget schedule in trimmed PDF. Read pages 1-13 of 13."
}